  "preamble": "The vowel [a] diphthongizes to [ai] through the insertion of a front glide. In standard Icelandic it is an allophonic rule: the monophthongs /a ɛ ɔ ʏ œ/ become short [i]-final diphthongs before ⟨gi⟩ [jɪ] within a morpheme, so hagi 'pasture' is [ˈhaijɪ].",
